[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5818132880","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123802#issuecomment-5818132880","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123802","id":5818132880,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABWsmpkA","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-24T16:33:33Z","updated_at":"2026-09-24T16:34:08Z","body":"This is as expected and [documented](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_scenetree.html#class-scenetree-method-quit):\n> Quits the application at the end of the current iteration\n\nI don't think anything is wrong here and changing this documented behavior would break compatibility\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5818132880/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5818190808","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123802#issuecomment-5818190808","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123802","id":5818190808,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABWsqL2A","user":{"login":"notroid5","id":87585310,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3NTg1MzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/87585310?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5","html_url":"https://github.com/notroid5","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-24T16:37:23Z","updated_at":"2026-09-24T16:37:23Z","body":"This seems rather unintuitive, though.\nI don't think any other language handles it like this.\n\nIn order to not break compatibility, could this be changed in 5.0?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5818190808/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5818220174","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123802#issuecomment-5818220174","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123802","id":5818220174,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABWsr-jg","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-24T16:39:24Z","updated_at":"2026-09-24T16:43:10Z","body":"It might be unintuitive but clearly documented, and I'd not expect the call to exit the current scope, no other method does\n\nI don't see why it would be changed, if someone is aware of this they should make sure their code makes sense, having code after the call to `quit` isn't really reasonable I'd say, just adding a `return` is simple enough\n\nFor code in other parts of the engine it would be a major breakage to make it stop working, for example code saving data when shutting, so that seems wrong too\n\nWe could make the error even more explicit by mentioning that code after the call will still execute, but I don't think that's justified\n\n> I don't think any other language handles it like this.\n\nThis isn't a language though it's an engine, so it's not really comparable, are you sure this is also the case in Unity or Unreal for example? This is not the same as the C++ `exit` function for example","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5818220174/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5818552342","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123802#issuecomment-5818552342","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123802","id":5818552342,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABWtAQFg","user":{"login":"notroid5","id":87585310,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3NTg1MzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/87585310?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5","html_url":"https://github.com/notroid5","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-24T17:02:01Z","updated_at":"2026-09-24T17:02:01Z","body":"Maybe I wasn't clear enough. I'm talking about GDScript, not the core engine.\n\nWhat I mean is that no further user code (by the project dev) should be executed. (Maybe unless they set something like `get_tree().set_auto_accept_quit(false)`.) So any custom script just stops. This shouldn't affect the engine, which can continue to quit as fast as possible.\n\n(Btw I checked anyway, Unreal has a way to force quit. But as that's not what I meant, just a FYI if you're curious. Couldn't find anything in Unity.)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5818552342/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":1,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5818659354","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123802#issuecomment-5818659354","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123802","id":5818659354,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABWtGyGg","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-24T17:09:26Z","updated_at":"2026-09-24T17:09:26Z","body":"That's what I mean, not sure where you got core engine from, I mean other code and contents. Other nodes will do their `_process` steps, this is as designed based on the documentation, so both the local scope (as in what your example code shows, which is what I based my response on, if you didn't mean that code is executed in the same code scope then the example is unclear) and other contexts will continue to process the current frame, as designed\n\n> But as that's not what I meant, just a FYI if you're curious\n\nWhat did you mean? You mentioned \"other languages\", so what do you mean by that? If you mean other ways to interact with the engine in Godot by calling this method then that is exactly the same","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5818659354/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5818812954","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123802#issuecomment-5818812954","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123802","id":5818812954,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABWtQKGg","user":{"login":"notroid5","id":87585310,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3NTg1MzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/87585310?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5","html_url":"https://github.com/notroid5","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-24T17:20:02Z","updated_at":"2026-09-24T17:20:02Z","body":"Then it's fine, just wanted to make sure we're on the same page.\n\nI mean \"other languages\" in general, not Godot-specific, like Node.js' `process.exit()`, or the C++ example you already gave.\nBut if GDScript isn't supposed to have a direct equivalent, I guess it works as intended.\n\nThanks for your fast responses!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5818812954/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]